# --- s044 Book I d.12 q.3 (uniform spiration) = Ord. I d.12 q.2
n("n725","s044-01","Tertia questio duodecime distinctionis","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 12 q. 2, *utrum Pater et Filius spirent Spiritum Sanctum uniformiter* (Vat. V). This is Gorris's third question because of the preceding question on *spiratores*.","to-verify")
n("n726","s044-01","Aug. 15. de trini. c. 7.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* XV 17.29 and 26.47: *de quo [Patre] procedit principaliter*. A's ‘c. 7’ is perhaps for c. 17 (B not checked).","to-verify")
n("n727","s044-02","Dum dicit soluendo argumenta principalia","la","textual","Thus also in B (*Dum dicit soluendo argumenta principalia*). The clause is elliptical and probably refers to Scotus's own reply to the principal arguments.","verified")
n("n728","s044-02","frater Alexander de Alexandria","la","historical","Alexander of Alessandria OFM (d. 1314), Franciscan minister general and commentator on the *Sentences*, I d. 12 q. 2.","to-verify")
n("n729","s044-02","sanctus Bonauentura. q. 2. in fi.","la","source","Bonaventure, *In I Sent.* d. 12 a. un. q. 2 (end) and *dubium* 3 *circa litteram*. On the Father as spirating *principalius*.","to-verify")
n("n730","s044-02","⟨Varronis⟩","la","textual","The initial is ambiguous in A (it resembles a G or S). B reads *Guilhel. var|ronis*, and A itself has *Guillermi varronis* at 046-02. This is William of Ware OFM (Guillelmus de Ware, ‘Varro/Guaro’; fl. c. 1290–1305), *In I Sent.* d. 12, Scotus's reputed teacher.","verified")
n("n731","s044-03","in eodem signo originis","la","source","Scotus's ‘signs (*signa*) of origin’: *Ord.* I d. 12 q. 2. In the first sign the Father has both fecundities from himself; in the second he generates and the Son has the second fecundity; in the third the Father and the Son spirate together.","to-verify")
n("n732","s044-04","in prima questione secundi latius","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* II d. 1 q. 1 (the *instantia/signa naturae* in the divine productions and in creation).","to-verify")
n("n733","s044-02","William ⟨Varro⟩","en","translation","See the Latin note: William of Ware.")

# --- B collation (full): B62L–B62R
upd("n726", text="Augustine, *De Trin.* XV 17.29 and 26.47: *de quo [Patre] procedit principaliter*. B reads only *Aug. 15. de tri.* without a chapter, so A's ‘c. 7’ has no support from B; perhaps for c. 17.")
upd("n730", append=" B confirms: *frater Guilhel. var|ronis in presenti dist.*")
